<title>NORWAY: Esso strikes oil off Norway, north of Bald.</title>
<headline>Esso strikes oil off Norway, north of Bald.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Norwegian Oil Directorate said on Wednesday that Esso Norge had found oil in license 027, block 25/8 in the North Sea.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that Esso, as operator, had completed drilling of exploration well 25/8-10 S, north of the Balder field, and that a production test was carried out.</p>
<p>&quot;The well tested at 413 cubic meters of oil per day and 14.7 cubic meters of gas per day through a 14.4 millimeter choke,&quot; the directorate said.</p>
<p>&quot;The size of the find and various means of development are under evaluation,&quot; the directorate said.</p>
<p>It said the find was interesting for further exploration in the area.</p>
<p>The well was drilled to a total depth of 1,859 metres in 128 metres of water.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
